        {
          "id": "p2",
          "text": "The power system operator faced a cascade of challenges as multiple plant outages compounded the crisis. Officials, acting as crisis navigators, ordered load shedding to protect the grid from overloading a critical transmission line. The emergency response was a necessary action to manage the energy deficit caused by high demand from the heatwave impact, leaving over 950 megawatts of power capacity unavailable in the region.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
            "fragments": [
              "why-1",
              "how-1",
              "how-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
